# Hand-edited config, deliberately separate from the secrets-managed .env so that bumping
# one date does not need a secrets write.
#
# Read by `docker run --env-file`, whose parser takes values LITERALLY: do NOT quote
# anything here. (The local dev .env read by `node --env-file` is the opposite — quote
# everything there. See README.)

# The last date you reconciled, YYYY-MM-DD. Rows on or before it are skipped, so a run
# never backfills an already-balanced account. Bump it when you reconcile — yesterday at the
# newest. A floor of today is refused: rows are skipped on <=, so it would discard the rest of
# today permanently, and tomorrow's sweep skips them again because the floor has not moved.
ACTUAL_MAIL_RECONCILED_THROUGH=2026-07-26

# Do NOT put ACTUAL_MAIL_DRY_RUN=1 in this file. A dry run is a command-line rehearsal (see the
# README quickstart); left here it stops every write on every scheduled run while the loader still
# exits 0. run.sh reads the loader's `dry run:` line and now fails the run rather than reporting a
# healthy one, so it is loud rather than silent — but the run still writes nothing.

# Failure alerts. Any service that accepts a JSON POST with a `content` field — Discord and
# Slack-compatible webhooks both do. Leave empty to disable; a clean run posts nothing
# either way.
ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Docker network to join, so the Actual server can be reached as a sibling container.
# Its externally-facing URL is NOT routable from inside a container — set the in-network
# URL here too, overriding whatever the secrets-managed .env carries.
ACTUAL_MAIL_NETWORK=bridge
# ACTUAL_SERVER_URL=http://actual-server:5006

# Push-style heartbeat (optional). Full URL for Uptime Kuma, Healthchecks.io, Cronitor or
# similar. `status` and `msg` are appended as query parameters. Unset = no heartbeat, and
# never a failed run.
HEARTBEAT_URL=
# Where to ping on FAILURE, if your monitor does not read a status parameter. Healthchecks.io
# needs this -- it signals failure with a /fail URL suffix and ignores unknown query parameters,
# so without it a failing run pings the success endpoint and marks the check UP. Leave empty for
# Uptime Kuma, which reads status=down off the URL above.
HEARTBEAT_FAIL_URL=
